# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers (framework-decision 9.4, pilot-decisions §7).
# Max 100 rules; not applied to responses generated by Worker code.
# index.html, sw.js and manifest.webmanifest keep Cloudflare's default
# (max-age=0, must-revalidate + ETag) so PWA updates are picked up.
# CSP (first deploy, Codex review 24.10): scripts only from our own origin (no inline script, no eval in the
# build — checked), no plugins, no <base>. Turnstile would need its script origin added here when switched on.
# Everything else (connect-src for Supabase, img-src for blob: photos) is not restricted yet.
# Framing (clickjacking, Codex review 2 L6) is allowed ONLY for Telegram Web, which shows the app as a
# Telegram Mini App in an iframe (Felix 24.10,
# docs/spec/telegram-mini-app.md §3.1); every other site is refused. No X-Frame-Options: it cannot
# express an allow-list and browsers ignore it once frame-ancestors is present. The dev phone frame is
# a DOM wrapper, not a frame.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://web.telegram.org https://webk.telegram.org https://weba.telegram.org; script-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'
/i
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/i/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
# Follow links /f#<code> (wave 2b, follows-design §2.9): like /i — never indexed, never a Referer (the code lives in
# the fragment and is moved to sessionStorage at once; no-referrer is repeated here on purpose, so the page keeps it
# even if the /* block changes).
/f
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
/f/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
